,{"languageCode":"cy","languageName":{"simpleText":"Welsh"}},{"languageCode":"fy","languageName":{"simpleText":"Western Frisian"}},{"languageCode":"wo","languageName":{"simpleText":"Wolof"}},{"languageCode":"xh","languageName":{"simpleText":"Xhosa"}},{"languageCode":"yi","languageName":{"simpleText":"Yiddish"}},{"languageCode":"yo","languageName":{"simpleText":"Yoruba"}},{"languageCode":"zu","languageName":{"simpleText":"Zulu"}}],"defaultAudioTrackIndex":8}},"videoDetails":{"videoId":"zRzDTrovOY0","title":"Amazing Onion Farming and Harvesting Techniques - Amazing Onion Cultivation","lengthSeconds":"470","keywords":["Onion Farming and Harvesting Techniques","Amazing Onion Farming and Harvesting Techniques - Amazing Onion Cultivation","Onion Farming","Onion Harvesting","Amazing Onion Harvesting","Onion Harvesting Techniques","Harvesting onion","onion Harvest","how to Harvest onion","Farming onion","onion","Onion Cultivation","onion Planting","Guide to Onion Farming","Amazing Farming Technology","farming","organic farming","how to start farming","Amazing Modern Automatic Farming Technology"],"channelId":"UC3OmAtvd-9AsBDEPIv9JeQQ","isOwnerViewing":false,"shortDescription":"Click Here To See :  Raisin,Dates,Walnut Processing  - https://youtu.be/6aCleihLoDA \nOnion Farming and Harvesting Techniques - Amazing Onion Farming\nOnion Farming, Planting, Care, Harvesting - A Full Guide, Amazing Modern Automatic Onion Farming Technology\n\nStart seeds indoors about 6 weeks before transplanting to the garden. Think of onions as a leaf crop, not a root crop. When planting onion sets, don't bury them more than 1 inch under the soil. For sets or transplants, space plants 4 to 5 inches apart in rows 12 to 18 inches apart.\n\nCredit : Media Plan and Gite Masdescombes and nitk7731\n\nIf you are the owner, please send me a email or comment on the video. I will follow your request as soon as i read. \n\n Please comment below , Which Cultivation and Farming video you need to watch ?\r\n\r\